  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Vankayala Hanuniantha Rao, vs The State Of Andhra Pradesh, on 12 September, 2019 Author: U. Durga Prasad Rao Bench: U. Durga Prasad Rao Hon'Ble Sri Justice U. Durga Prasad Rao Criminal Petition No.4978 Of 2019 Order:",
    "facts": "The petitioner/accused seeks to quash the proceedings against him in C.C.No.250 of 2018 in Crime No.14 of 2018 of Karamchedu Police Station, Prakasam District, which was registered against him for the offences under Sections 273, 188 of IPC and Sec.58 of Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 (for short 'FSS Act, 2006). 2. The allegations against the petitioner briefly are that on 30.01.2018 the SI of Police, on credible information raided the wholesale shop of the petitioner at Audipudi Village, Karamchedu Mandal and arrested the petitioner while he was selling the prohibited tobacco products like Khaini, Panparag, gutka etc., and seized banned products under a panchanama. Later, he registered the same as a case in Crime No.14 of 2018 for the offences stated supra. 3.",
    "arguments": "Learned counsel for petitioner while denying the FIR allegations would submit that even if the prosecution case is accepted to be true, tobacco products would not fall within the definition of Section 3(j) of FSS Act and therefore, the Police are not authorized to register the crime, investigate and file charge sheet and therefore, registration of the FIR is contrary to the provisions of FSS Act.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned counsel for petitioner while denying the FIR allegations would submit that even if the prosecution case is accepted to be true, tobacco products would not fall within the definition of Section 3(j) of FSS Act and therefore, the Police are not authorized to register the crime, investigate and file charge sheet and therefore, registration of the FIR is contrary to the provisions of FSS Act.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
